WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.710
Jane Foster's wielding the magical hammer
Mjolnir, but she's also sporting some impressive arm muscles.

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:07.839
Are these guns connected to Mjolnir's return?

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.950
And how did Jane get her newly-jacked hands
on Thor's old hammer anyway?

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:15.590
Warning: spoilers ahead for "Thor: Love and
Thunder!"

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.439
Directed by Taika Waititi, "Thor: Love and
Thunder" has finally hit theaters, complete

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:23.990
with a brand new villain, numerous references
to mythology, and some screaming goats.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:28.659
The narrative also reintroduces viewers to
Dr. Jane Foster whose presence is instrumental

00:00:28.659 --> 00:00:32.940
in helping Thor and King Valkyrie battle against
an evil that threatens the future of New Asgard.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:36.230
Ever since the first trailer dropped, fans
have been clamoring to find out what leads

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.330
the astrophysicist to become Mighty Thor and
how she came to possess Thor's old hammer.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.690
At this point in the franchise, Mjolnir is
practically a character all its own.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:48.910
The hammer's resurrection brings about a host
of changes, significantly influencing Thor's

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.630
journey to self-discovery.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.160
After years of letting us wonder, "Thor: Love
and Thunder" finally explains why Thor and

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:55.890
Jane went their separate ways.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.700
For an astrophysicist and the God of thunder,
the pair managed to build a strong foundation

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.700
for a future together.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.368
Everything was good for a while, but the differences
in their lives eventually drove a wedge between them.

00:01:05.368 --> 00:01:08.759
As it turns out, it's not easy building a
life with someone who's always running off

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:11.270
to face intergalactic threats.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.469
Thor couldn't cope with his fear of losing
her, so he embraced the growing distance in

00:01:14.469 --> 00:01:15.689
their relationship.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:19.609
In the end, it was Jane who pulled the plug
on their romance, even if Thor has trouble

00:01:19.609 --> 00:01:20.609
admitting it.

00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:22.509
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:24.790
"She didn't dump me.

00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:25.899
I dumped her.

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:27.670
It was a mutual dumping."

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.170
Following the events of "Avengers: Endgame,"
Thor is back to his old self with the help

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:35.159
of a strict workout regime and some quality
time with the Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:38.420
He hasn't seen Jane in years, but that's about
to change.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:42.100
Jane's life has changed dramatically since
viewers last saw her in "Thor: The Dark World."

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:46.130
In Thor's absence, she's had plenty of time
to focus on her career.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.920
Unfortunately, Jane discovers that she has
stage 4 cancer and her prognosis isn't looking good.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.359
Although Darcy and Dr. Selvig have attempted
to convince her to save her energy, Jane has

00:01:55.359 --> 00:01:58.159
been tirelessly working to find a way to cure
herself.

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:02.270
Reaching the end of her rope, Jane finds herself
drawn to tales from Norse mythology.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:06.350
Although Thor and the other Asgardians aren't
immortal, a fact cemented by Loki's death

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.429
at the hands of Thanos, they don't fall victim
to the same frailties that affect humans.

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:14.549
Their magic grants them a certain level of
invulnerability, including super strength

00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:15.549
and good health.

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:19.340
These aspects of godliness intrigue Jane,
but there's more to it than that.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:24.340
Thor's hammer Mjolnir has always been a conduit
for this power and it calls out to Jane.

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:26.569
Flashbacks demonstrate that this is no accident.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:31.129
As their relationship dwindled, Thor asked
Mjolnir to watch over Jane, a magical request

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:32.930
that has remained intact.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:36.763
Even after all these years, Thor and Jane
are still connected, whether they know it or not.

00:02:36.763 --> 00:02:40.879
In a last-ditch effort to cure her cancer,
Jane travels to New Asgard, which has become

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:42.680
a major tourist attraction.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.840
After being destroyed by Hela in "Thor: Ragnarok,"
the broken pieces of Mjolnir are on display

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.390
in a glass case.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:52.060
Since its destruction, everyone has assumed
that Mjolnir was beyond repair.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:55.930
For the relocated Asgardians, the shattered
relic reminds them of where they came from

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:58.690
and all they've faced since the decimation
of their home world.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.939
For sightseers, it's the physical embodiment
of one of Earth's mightiest heroes.

00:03:02.939 --> 00:03:07.070
For Jane, it's her last hope for survival,
a doorway to a life where her illness is a

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.709
thing of the past.

00:03:08.709 --> 00:03:12.250
All this time, Mjolnir was waiting for Jane
and she is more than worthy.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:16.790
As promised, Mjolnir grants Jane the powers
of a god, resulting in the effortlessly cool,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.930
muscled-up version of the character fans have
seen in trailers.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.159
Unfortunately, wielding the hammer isn't enough
to save Jane, who dies helping Thor defeat

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:25.210
Gor the God Butcher.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.840
Her sacrifice has a profound effect on Thor,
who is finally able to accept his past and

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.220
look towards a brighter future, Mjolnir in
hand.

